Template Column Heading,Data type,Summary,,,,
,      DATA CATEGORISATION ,,,,,
confidentiality_status,Dropdown list,"To be used in future iterations if required to record whether data is published, unpublished or a combination.  Currently all data on VA platform will be published data.",,,,
bio_data,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Does the data row include bionomics data?,,,,
adult_data,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Does the data row include data on adult mosquitoes?,,,,
larval_site_data,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Does the data row include data on mosquito larval sites,,,,
insecticide_resistance_data,Dropdown list,"Does the data row include insecticide resistance data and if so, is it phenotypic, genotypic or both. If no IR data present, select ‘none’",,,,
,,,,,,
,      SOURCE INFORMATION,,,,,
source_id,Alphanumerical,Unique Vector Atlas source identifier ,,,,
citation_doi,Alphanumerical,"Unique Digital Object Identifier from the source. This maybe the journal article, or the DOI for a published dataset",,,,
author,Character,Surname of first author,,,,
article_title,Alphanumerical,Full article title,,,,
journal_title,Alphanumerical,Full journal title,,,,
publication_year,Numeric,Year the article was published,,,,
study_sampling_design,Dropdown list,Enter the study or sampling design if provided by author. Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions.,,,,
personal_communication,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Is this data row source personal communication?,,,,
contact_authors,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Is there potential to obtain further information by contacting the author?,,,,
source_notes,Alphanumerical,Free text additional information about the source and details of reason to contact author.,,,,
,,,,,,
,     SITE AND GEOREFERENCING,,,,,
country,Character,Country where the study was conducted,,,,
site,Alphanumerical,Site name where the mosquito sample was collected.,,,,
latitude_1,Numeric,Latitude of first site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_1,Numeric,Longitude of first site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_2,Numeric,Latitude of second site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_2,Numeric,Longitude of second site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_3,Numeric,Latitude of third site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_3,Numeric,Longitude of third site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_4,Numeric,Latitude of fourth site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_4,Numeric,Longitude of fourth site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_5,Numeric,Latitude of fifth site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_5,Numeric,Longitude of fifth site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_6,Numeric,Latitude of sixth site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_6,Numeric,Longitude of sixth site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_7,Numeric,Latitude of seventh site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_7,Numeric,Longitude of seventh site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
latitude_8,Numeric,Latitude of eighth site coordinates in decimal degrees,,,,
longitude_8,Numeric,Longitude of eighth site coordinates in decimal degrees.,,,,
confidence_in_georef,Dropdown list,The data abstractor assigns confidence in the location of the coordinates they have estimated: within 5km / between 5 - 10km / greater than 10km. We use this field only where the site cannot be found in a georeferencing source and when we are estimating the coordinates using a map or peripheral site information in the source.,,,,
area_type,Dropdown list,The geographical area represented by the sampling location(s). Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions.,,,,
georef_source,Dropdown list,"When the site name and corresponding coordinates have been found listed in the original article, source of data or from a mapping resource and its location confirmed to be accurate, indicate from which resource the site was found (e.g., the original paper, google maps, etc.).",,,,
admin_level_1,Character,"The highest administration level after Country. In Africa, this may be Region, Province, District, Division etc. (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_administrative_divisions_by_country).",,,,
admin_level_2,Character,The highest administration level after Admin level_1. ,,,,
site_notes,Alphanumerical,Free text additional information about the site and how co-ordinates were obtained.,,,,
,,,,,,
,       INSECTICIDE BASED CONTROL,,,,,
insecticide_control,Dropdown list,Yes/No/Na. Indicate whether insecticide-based control methods are in place (previously implemented or implemented as part of the referenced study) at the specified location and for the specified time period.  ,,,,
control_type,Dropdown list,"If ‘yes’ to insecticide control field, indicate the insecticide control method. Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions",,,,
itn_use,Dropdown list,"Yes/No/Na. Where ITNs have been distributed, they may not always be used, especially during the warmer months. Indicate here if the source indicates good or non-use in the study community. ",,,,
control_notes,Dropdown list,Free text additional information about the insecticide control,,,,
,,,,,,
,       OCCURRENCE/ABUNDANCE SAMPLING,,,,,
sampling_occurrence_1,Dropdown list,The sampling method reported that generated the most mosquitoes,,,,
occurrence_n_1,Numeric,"The number of mosquitoes reported for sampling occurrence_1. If the sampling method DID NOT CATCH specimens from a species, report it here by listing ‘0’.",,,,
sampling_occurrence_2,Dropdown list,The sampling method reported that generated the second most mosquitoes,,,,
occurrence_n_2,Numeric,"The number of mosquitoes reported for sampling occurrence_2. If the sampling method DID NOT CATCH specimens from a species, report it here by listing ‘0’.",,,,
sampling_occurrence_3,Dropdown list,The sampling method reported that generated the third most mosquitoes,,,,
occurrence_n_3,Numeric,"The number of mosquitoes reported for sampling occurrence_3. If the sampling method DID NOT CATCH specimens from a species, report it here by listing ‘0’.",,,,
sampling_occurrence_4,Dropdown list,The sampling method reported that generated the fourth most mosquitoes ,,,,
occurrence_n_4,Numeric,"The number of mosquitoes reported for sampling occurrence_4. If the sampling method DID NOT CATCH specimens from a species, report it here by listing ‘0’.",,,,
occurrence_n_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes reported for all sampling methods,,,,
occurrence_notes,Alphanumerical,"Where there are more than three sampling methods, report any additional ones in the notes alongside the number of mosquitoes collected, including where no mosquitoes were captured.",,,,
binary_presence,Dropdown list,"Yes/no. Indicate ‘yes’ if the source indicates the presence of a species at the given time and place (i.e., that data row), even if we have positive numbers in the n_1, n_2, or n-3 columns.",,,,
binary_absence,Dropdown list,"Yes/no. Indicate ‘yes’ if the source indicates the absence of a species at the given time and place (i.e., that data row) for all sampling methods used in the study.",,,,
abundance_data_in_a_graph,Dropdown list,"Yes/no/na. We do not estimate numbers collected from graphs in the source. However, indicate here if there is such a graph in the source so we can go back to the author and ask for the raw data.",,,,
,,,,,,
,       SAMPLING PERIOD,,,,,
month_start,Numeric,Survey start month.,,,,
month_end,Numeric,Survey end month.,,,,
year_start,Numeric,Survey start year.,,,,
year_end,Numeric,Survey end year.,,,,
season_given,Dropdown list,"Rainy or dry season at the time of the survey, as indicated in the source",,,,
season_calc,Dropdown list,"Rainy or dry season at the time of the survey, as derived from information on the general seasonal timings provided from the source or elsewhere",,,,
rainfall_time,Alphanumerical,"If the source provides information on the level of rainfall that relates to the time period represented in the sampling period shown, then enter it here. It must match the time period represented on that row.",,,,
season_notes,Alphanumerical,Note anything here that relates to how you calculated the season.,,,,
,,,,,,
,,,,,,
,       SPECIES,,,,,
species,Dropdown list,"The Anopheles species, species complex or subgroup. The drop-down list contains the most common African vectors listed first and then the remaining Anopheles species listed alphabetically. Accurately represent the species information as given, noting the cases outlined in the box on page 2 of the VA Protocol. ",,,,
species_notes,Alphanumerical,"Note here anything that relates to the species or its identification, including any mention of additional molecular or chromosomal forms. However, the species listed must always accurately represent the data as we will search the data by species and not necessarily see the notes unless checking some query. ",, ,,
species_id_1,Dropdown list,The first method used to identify species. Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions.,,,,
species_id_2,Dropdown list,The second method used to identify species. Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions.,,,,
,,,,,,
,       HOUSING,,,,,
roof,Dropdown list,"List if the majority of homes have a metal or thatched roof, or use ‘mix’ if there is a mix of metal and thatch in the study/survey area. Anything else, list as ‘other’ and give details in the housing notes. If no information is provided, leave blank.",,,,
walls,Dropdown list,"List if the majority of homes have brick or mud walls, or use ‘mix’ if there is a mix of brick and mud in the study area. Anything else, list as ‘other’ and give details in the housing notes. If no information is provided, leave blank.",,,,
house_screening,Dropdown list,Add yes/no if the source indicates the majority of homes in the study area have or do not have screening (on windows and doors). Give details in the housing notes column.,,,,
open_eaves,Dropdown list,Add yes/no if the source indicates the majority of homes in the study area have or do not have open eaves. Give details in the housing notes column.,,,,
cooking,Dropdown list,"List if the source indicates that the majority of homes in the survey area cook indoors or outdoors, and if further detail is given as to the use of open fires (inside or outside). If no information is provided, leave blank.",,,,
housing_notes,Alphanumerical,"Add notes that relate to any housing metric captured or any other details that may be relevant to vector access to homes, disease transmission etc.",,,,
,,,,,,
,       COMMUNITY,,,,,
common_occupation_1,Dropdown list,List any occupations as given in the source that best represent the sampling area referred to in the specific data row.,,,,
common_occupation_2,Dropdown list,List any occupations as given in the source that best represent the sampling area referred to in the specific data row.,,,,
common_occupation_3,Dropdown list,"List any occupations as given in the source that best represent the sampling area referred to in the specific data row. If there are more than three occupations, or the occupation is not listed, use the ‘community notes’ column.",,,,
outdoor_activities_at_night,Dropdown list,"Yes/No/Na. List ‘yes’ if the source reports that the community regularly engage in activities outdoors at night (socialising, watching sport, watch TV etc) during the period represented on the data row. List ‘no’ if the source specifically states the community does not engage in outdoor activities at night during the period of time indicated in the data row. Provide details in the ‘outdoor activities notes’ column. Leave blank if no information related to outdoor activities are reported.",,,,
sleeping_outdoors,Dropdown list,Yes/No/Na. Indicate ‘yes’ if the source reports the community regularly sleeps outdoors during the period represented on the data row. List ‘no’ if the source specifically states the community does not sleep outdoors at night during the period of time indicated in the data row.,,,,
outdoor_timings_hours,Alphanumerical,Provide details of the times (in 24-hour clock) or number of hours spent outdoors when provided by the source.,,,,
outdoor_activities_notes,Alphanumerical,Provide any details of any outdoor activities given in the preceding columns that may be relevant to malaria transmission/vector activity at night. ,,,,
average_bedtime,Numeric - 24 hour clock,"Where given in the source, list the average bedtime of the community represented in the data row. Use 24-hour clock format.",,,,
average_wake_time,Numeric - 24 hour clock,"Where given in the source, list the average awake time of the community represented in the data row. Use 24-hour clock format.",,,,
time_people_leave_home_in_morning,Numeric - 24 hour clock,"Where given in the source, list the average time members of the community represented in the data row leave their homes in the day. Use 24-hour clock format.",,,,
hours_spent_away_from_home_per_day,Numeric,"Where given in the source, list the average time members of the community represented in the data row are away from home during the day. ",,,,
seasonal_labour,Dropdown list,"Yes/No/Na. List ‘yes’ if the source indicates that significant numbers of the community represented in the data line engage in seasonal labour, i.e., leave their homes for a season to work in forestry, agriculture etc. Provide details in the community notes column.",,,,
community_notes,Alphanumerical,List any details that relate to the entries in the community section. ,,,,
,,,,,,
,   ENVIRONMENT,,,,,
forest,Dropdown list,Yes/no/na. Does the source indicate forest in the sampling location?,,,,
farming,Dropdown list,Does the source indicate forest in the sampling location? Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options. ,,,,
farming_notes,Alphanumerical,Add any information here that relates to farming practices at the location/time relating to the data row. ,,,,
livestock_1,Dropdown list,"List the livestock in the area that relates to the data row as given by the source (cattle, goats, chickens, horses, dogs, cats, pigs, combination, other, na).",,,,
livestock_2,Dropdown list,List the livestock in the area that relates to the data row as given by the source.,,,,
livestock_3,Dropdown list,List the livestock in the area that relates to the data row as given by the source.,,,,
livestock_4,Dropdown list,List the livestock in the area that relates to the data row as given by the source.,,,,
livestock_notes,Alphanumerical,"If there are more than four species of livestock provided by the source, list additional animal species here. Add any details relevant to the impact of livestock on malaria transmission.",,,,
local_plants,Alphanumerical,List all the species of plants mentioned in the source that relate to the location/site in the data row.,,,,
environment_notes,Alphanumerical,Add any relevant information or detail about the local ecology or environment that are relevant to vector ecology/bionomics/disease transmission.,,,,
,,,,,,
,   BIOLOGY,,,,,
sampling_biology_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the specimens detailed in the BIOLOGY section. Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the sampling_biology_n column.",,,,
sampling_biology_2,Dropdown list,As ‘sampling_biology_1’.,,,,
sampling_biology_3,Dropdown list,As ‘sampling_biology_1’.,,,,
sampling_biology_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods.,,,,
parity_n,Numeric,The number of parous females detected from the total number examined.,,,,
parity_total,Numeric,The total number of females examined for parity.,,,,
parity_percent,Numeric,The percentage of parous females in the sample: = number of parous females/total number examined x 100.,,,,
daily_survival_rate_percent,Numeric,The estimated proportion of female mosquitoes alive on day d that are still alive on day d+1.,,,,
fecundity_mean_batch_size,Numeric,The number of eggs laid per batch.,,,,
gonotrophic_cycle_days,Numeric,The number of days for a female mosquito to go through the reproduce-feeding cycle.,,,,
biology_notes,Alphanumerical,Free text additional information about the vector biology.,,,,
,,,,,,
,   INFECTION,,,,,
sampling_infection_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the specimens detailed in the VECTOR INFECTION RATE section. Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the final column. ",,,,
sampling_infection_2,Dropdown list,As ‘sampling_infection_1’,, ,,
sampling_infection_3,Dropdown list,As ‘sampling_infection_1’,,,,
sampling_infection_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods,,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_dissection_n,Numeric,The number of sporozoite positive mosquitoes detected by dissection,,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_dissection_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes dissected,,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_dissection_percent,Numeric,The sporozoite rate (percent) = SRn/SRtotal x 100 from dissection,,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_csp_n_pool,Numeric,The number of sporozoite positive mosquitoes detected by circumsporozoite protein (CSP)in a sample (pool),,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_csp_total_pool,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes inThe pool (sample) tested by CSP,,,,
sporozoite_rate_by_csp_percent,Numeric,The sporozoite rate (percent) = SRn_pool/SRtotal_pool x 100 from CSP,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_falciparum_n,Numeric,The number of P. falciparum sporozoite positive mosquitoes detected by CSP in a sample.,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_falciparum_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes in the pool (sample) tested by CSP for P. falciparum sporozoites.,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_falciparum_percent,Numeric,The P. falciparum sporozoite rate (percent) = PfSRnl/PfSRtotal x 100 from CSP.,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_vivax_n,Numeric,The number of P. vivax sporozoite positive mosquitoes detected by CSP in a sample.,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_vivax_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes in the pool (sample) tested by CSP for P. vivax sporozoites.,,,,
sporozoite_rate_p_vivax_percent,Numeric,The P. vivax sporozoite rate (percent) = PvSRnl/PvSRtotal x 100 from CSP. ,,,,
oocyst_n,Numeric,The number of oocyst infected females detected from the total number examined.,, ,,
oocyst_total,Numeric,The total number of females examined for oocysts.,,,,
oocyst_rate_percent,Numeric,The percentage of oocyst infected females detected in the sample: = number of infected females/total number examined x 100.,,,,
eir,Numeric,The entomological inoculation rate.,,,,
eir_period,Dropdown list,"The unit of time relating to the EIR (day, week, month, year).",,,,
ext_incubation_period_days,Numeric,The extrinsic incubation period of the malaria parasite in days.,,,,
infection_notes,Alphanumerical,Any additional details or information relating to the infection status of the mosquito species at the time and place given in the data row,,,,
,,,,,,
,   HUMAN BITING RATE,,,,,
hbr_sampling_indoor,Dropdown list,The sampling method used to collect the mosquitoes from which indoor human biting rate is evaluated. As ‘sampling_biology_1’.,,,,
indoor_hbr,Numeric,The indoor human biting rate; the number of bites per person per unit time.,,,,
hbr_sampling_outdoor,Dropdown list,The sampling method used to collect the mosquitoes from which outdoor human biting rate is evaluated. As ‘sampling_biology_1’.,,,,
outdoor_hbr,Numeric,The outdoor human biting rate; the number of bites per person per unit time.,,,,
hbr_sampling_combined_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the mosquitoes from which human biting rate is evaluated where data are amalgamated from more than one method (e.g., where HBRs are given from combined indoor and outdoor sampling methods, or where the method used is unclear). Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the hbr sampling_combined_n column. As ‘_sampling_biology_1’.",,,,
hbr_sampling_combined_2,Dropdown list,As ‘hbr sampling_combined_1’.,,,,
hbr_sampling_combined_3,Dropdown list,As ‘hbr sampling_combined_1’.,,,,
hbr_sampling_combined_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods.,,,,
combined_hbr,Numeric,The human biting rate evaluated from the data from amalgamated sampling methods.,,,,
hbr_unit,Dropdown list,The unit time for the HBR data.,,,,
abr_sampling_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the mosquitoes from which the animal biting rate is evaluated where data are amalgamated from more than one method (e.g., where ABRs are given from combined indoor and outdoor sampling methods, or where the method used is unclear). Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the abr sampling_n column.",,,,
abr_sampling_2,Dropdown list,As ‘abr sampling_1’,,,,
abr_sampling_3,Dropdown list,As ‘abr sampling_1’,,,,
abr_sampling_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods,,,,
abr,Numeric,The animal biting rate evaluated from the data from amalgamated sampling methods.,,,,
abr_unit,Dropdown list,The unit time for the ABR data.,,,,
biting_rate_notes,Alphanumerical, Free text additional information about the human and animal biting rates,,,,
,,,,,,
,   VECTOR HOST PREFERENCE,,,,,
host_sampling_indoor,Dropdown list,The indoor sampling method used to collect the mosquitoes from which indoor host preference is evaluated. As ‘sampling_biology_1.,,,,
indoor_host_n,Numeric,The number of mosquitoes positively indicating a measure of host preference fromThe total number collected indoors,,,,
indoor_host_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes sampled indoors examined for measures of host preference,,,,
indoor_host_percent,Numeric,The measure of host preference from indoor sampled mosquitoes,,,,
host_sampling_outdoor,Dropdown list,The outdoor sampling method used to collectThe mosquitoes from which outdoor host preference is evaluated,,,,
outdoor_host_n,Numeric,The number of mosquitoes positively indicating a measure of host preference fromThe total number collected outdoors,,,,
outdoor_host_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes sampled outdoors examined for measures of host preference,,,,
outdoor_host_percent,Numeric,The measure of host preference from outdoor sampled mosquitoes,,,,
host_sampling_combined_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the mosquitoes from which host preference is evaluated where data are amalgamated from more than one method, or where the method used is unclear. Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the final column. As ‘sampling_biology_1’.",,,,
host_sampling_combined_2,Dropdown list,As ‘host sampling_combined_1.,, As ‘sampling_biology_1’,,
host_sampling_combined_3,Dropdown list,As ‘host sampling_combined_1.,,,,
host_sampling_combined_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods.,,,,
combined_host_n,Numeric,The number of mosquitoes positively indicating a measure of host preference collected by a combination of sampling methods.,,,,
combined_host_total,Numeric,"The total number of mosquitoes sampled by a combination of sampling methods, examined for measures of host preference.",,,,
combined_host,Dropdown list,The measure of host preference from mosquitoes sampled by a combination of methods.,,,,
host_unit,Dropdown list,Indicates the measure used to identify host preference. Refer to the ‘Definitions’ tab of the abstraction template for a list of the options and definitions.,,,,
host_sampling_other_1,Dropdown list,"The sampling methods used to collect the mosquitoes from which host preference is evaluated where additional data are presented examining host preference. Three methods can be listed. If more than three methods have been used, this is indicated as 'yes' in the final column. ",,,,
host_sampling_other_2,Dropdown list,As ‘host sampling_other_1’.,, ,,
host_sampling_other_3,Dropdown list,As ‘host sampling_other_1’.,,,,
host_sampling_other_n,Dropdown list,‘Yes’ indicates that there are more than three sampling methods.,,,,
other_host_n,Numeric,The number of mosquitoes positively indicating a measure of host preference.,,,,
other_host_total,Numeric,The total number of mosquitoes examined for measures of host preference.,,,,
host_other,Numeric,The measure of host preference.,,,,
host_other_unit,Dropdown list,As ‘host_unit’.,,,,
host_notes,Alphanumerical,Free text additional information about the host notes.,,,,
