,   INSECTICIDE RESISTANCE BIOASSAYS,,,,,
bioassay_representative_of_complex_at_site,Dropdown list,Yes/no. A representative sample is a random sample that is representative of the population of interest. Is the mosquito population utilised for the susceptibility test representative of the complex at the site?,,,,
bioassay_representative_of_complex_at_site_if_disaggregated_values_combined_without_adjustments,Dropdown list,"Yes/no. Multiple rows of data would be representative if disaggregated values were combined. For example, if individual species values were combined to give result as the complex.  ",,,,
generation,Dropdown list,"The mosquito generation tested: F0, F1 or a mix of both. F0: wild caught adults or wild caught larvae that were reared to adults before testing.  F1: first generation offspring of wild caught adults or larvae. ",,  ,,
wild_caught_larvae_or_adults,Dropdown list,Whether the mosquito was caught as an adult or caught as larvae and raised to adult for testing.,, ,,
lower_age_days,Numeric,Lower age in days if age range given for mosquito (e.g. 3 if 3-5 days).,,,,
upper_age_days,Numeric,"Upper age in days, if age range given for mosquito (e.g., 5 if 3-5 days).",,,,
test_protocol,Dropdown list,The WHO or CDC bioassay protocol followed is listed by organisation and publication year.,,,,
insecticide_tested,Dropdown list,The insecticide tested is named.,,,,
insecticide_class,Dropdown list,The chemical class the insecticide tested belongs to as per drop down list.,,,,
irac_moa,Dropdown list,Insecticide Resistance Action Committee (IRAC) mode of action (MoA) as per drop down list. See IRAC Classification website for details. https://irac-online.org/mode-of-action/classification-online/ ,,,,
irac_moa_code,Dropdown list,"Number letter code of the IRAC MoA e.g., 1A. Refer toIRAC Classification website. https://irac-online.org/mode-of-action/classification-online/ ",,,,
concentration_percent,Numeric,"If a WHO protocol was followed, the insecticide concentration is given as a percent.",,,,
concentration_micrograms,Numeric,"If the CDC protocol was followed, the insecticide concentration is given in μg/bottle.",,,,
exposure_period_min,Numeric,The period of time the mosquitoes are exposed to the insecticide in minutes.,,,,
intensity_multiplier,Numeric,"The number by which the recommended or baseline insecticide concentration is multiplied If several tests are done exposing mosquitoes to an insecticide at different dose concentrations (intensity bioassays), then enter ‘1’ for the baseline/standard concentration and the appropriate multiplied number for higher concentrations, e.g. if standard dose is 0.75%, then enter ‘2’ for a concentration of 1.5%.",,,,
synergist_tested,Dropdown list,The synergist tested is named for susceptibility tests where mosquitoes are exposed to a synergist as well as the insecticide.  Leave blank if no synergist used.,,,,
synergist_concentration,Numeric,The synergist concentration is given.,,,,
synergist_concentration_unit,Dropdown list,The concentration unit is recorded depending on whether CDC or WHO test procedures.,,,,
mosquitoes_tested_n,Dropdown list,The total number of mosquitoes tested in all replicates.,,,,
mosquitoes_dead_n,Dropdown list,"The total number of mosquitoes tested in all replicates. If range given, e.g. 80-100 mosquitoes tested, enter the lowest value of range, e.g. 80, and put range in bioassay notes. ",,,,
percent_mortality,Dropdown list,"The percentage of mosquitoes that died across all replicates, adjusted using Abbot’s formula if applicable.",,,,
knock_down_exposure_time_min,Numeric,The period of exposure to the insecticide in minutes before knock down recorded.,,,,
mosquitoes_knocked_down_n,Numeric,Number of mosquitoes knocked down at recorded exposure time.,,,,
knock_down_percent,Numeric,Percentage of mosquitoes knocked down at recorded exposure time.,,,,
kdt_50_percent_min,Numeric,The time it takes to knock down 50% of the mosquito sample.,,,,
kdt_90_percent_min,Numeric,The time it takes to knock down 90% of the mosquito sample.,,,,
kdt_95_percent_min,Numeric,The time it takes to knock down 95% of the mosquito sample.,,,,
bioassay_notes,Alphanumerical,Free text additional information about the bioassay tests.,,,,
,,,,,,
,   GENETIC MECHANISMS LINKS,,,,,
genotypic_test_representative_of_species_at_site,Dropdown list,Yes/no. A representative sample is a random sample that is representative of the population of interest.  Is the mosquito population utilised for the genotypic test representative of the species at the site?,,,,
genotypic_test_representative_of_species_at_site_if_disaggregated_values_combined_without_adjustments,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Multiple rows of data would be representative if disaggregated values were combined. ,,,,
minor_species_missing_allele_frequency_data,Dropdown list,Yes/no.  Indicate ‘yes’ if minor species identified but genetic mechanism data for that species is not reported.,,,,
notes_on_population_representative,Alphanumerical,Free text for additional information related to sample representativeness.,,,,
genotypic_sample_first_been_through_bioassay_tests,Dropdown list,Yes/no.  Did the sample first go through bioassay testing before being selected for genotypic tests?  Including pooled samples from multiple bioassays.,,,,
genotypic_sample_linked_to_a_specific_bioassay,Dropdown list,Yes/no. Indicate ‘yes’ if the sample used in the genetic mechanisms tests matches to a specific bioassay test (not a pooled sample but linked to a specific insecticide tested).,,,,
bioassay_subsample_used_in_genotypic_test,Dropdown list,"What subsample of mosquitoes from the bioassay test were utilised in genotypic tests: dead only, alive only, dead and alive or not specified?",,,,
notes_on_bioassay_linkage,Dropdown list,Free text for additional information related to bioassay matching to the genetic mechanisms. ,,,,
